In terms of technology proposals, the most exciting proposals comes from
the vacuum eclctronics arena (session 7). A team of researchers from the
Los Alamos National Laboratory, Los Alamos, New Mexico proposes to build an
RF accelerator that will bombard long lived nuclear waste, dropping the
waste's half life to about 30 years. The accelerator will require klystrons
